  "notes": [
    {
      "level": "verify",
      "at": "paint[kind=warning]",
      "message": "WarningFilled and WarningAltFilled are two-tone: _toast-notification.scss L221-L229 paints the inner mark (path[opacity='0'], path:first-of-type) $black-100 while the outer shape takes $support-warning-inverse. Icons are one flattened Vector (#13), so the Design Library shows the mark cut out instead of black."
    },
    {
      "level": "verify",
      "at": "layout.Toast notification",
      "message": "Carbon's box-shadow 0 2px 6px 0 rgb(0 0 0 / 0.2) (_toast-notification.scss L38) is not drawn: the builder writes a raw effect colour without alpha, and Carbon's shadow token (alpha 0.3) is not scoped EFFECT_COLOR. Add it by hand in Figma, or as a token once Foundations has one."
    },
    {
      "level": "verify",
      "at": "anatomy.Icon",
      "message": "The status icons render at size={20} (Notification.tsx L295). @carbon/icons 11.90.0 has no svg/20, so the Design Library scales the svg/16 glyph (error--filled, checkmark--filled, warning--filled) or the svg/32 fallback (information--filled, information--square--filled, warning--alt--filled) to icon-size-02."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "anatomy.Accent",
      "message": "The 3px start border (_mixins.scss L35, notification--experimental) is its own FRAME, as a border on one side is (ADR 0013). It and the status icon take the kind colour: support-<kind>-inverse, with info and info-square sharing support-info-inverse and warning and warning-alt sharing support-warning-inverse (_toast-notification.scss L185-L214)."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "layout.Details.paddingBottom",
      "message": "Carbon renders title, subtitle and caption only when given (Notification.tsx L475-L489). The Contract always shows Title and Subtitle; the spacing is the title-and-subtitle case: the title's margin-block-start $spacing-05 (L287) on top, the subtitle's margin-block-end $spacing-05 (L295) and the details' $spacing-05 (L238) below."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "layout.Toast notification.width",
      "message": "At the max breakpoint (1584px) the toast is 352px wide (_toast-notification.scss L43-L45). The Contract draws the 288px default."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "anatomy.Close button",
      "message": "The close button is transparent with a 2px $focus-inverse outline on :focus (_toast-notification.scss L273-L276). The toast has no State axis: its states are the close button's, which is not a family of its own."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "family",
      "message": "Left out of this draft: lowContrast (its notification-background-* tokens are not in the Foundations), caption (its padding-block-start $spacing-03 needs a gap the title and subtitle do not have), hideCloseButton (a BOOLEAN shows a node when true, and this prop hides it), role, timeout, actions and children, and the v12 border radius behind enable-v12-release."
    }
  ],
